It must compute: out[i, j] = u[i] * v[j] for all i, j (outer product).

Relevant operations: broadcast_in_dim, element-wise ops (add/subtract/multiply/divide/maximum/minimum/negate/exponential/sqrt/rsqrt/abs).

Reply with the complete program in a single ```mlir code block.

```mlir
// StableHLO program to compute outer product of two vectors u and v
module {
  func.func @main(%u: tensor<3xf32>, %v: tensor<4xf32>) -> tensor<3x4xf32> {
    // Broadcast %u to shape [3,4], broadcasting along dimension 1
    %u_bcast = "stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim"(%u) {
      broadcast_dimensions = [0, 1]
    } : (tensor<3xf32>) -> tensor<3x4xf32>

    // Broadcast %v to shape [3,4], broadcasting along dimension 0
    %v_bcast = "stablehlo.broadcast_in_dim"(%v) {
      broadcast_dimensions = [1, 0]
    } : (tensor<4xf32>) -> tensor<3x4xf32>

    // Element-wise multiply the broadcasted tensors
    %out = "stablehlo.multiply"(%u_bcast, %v_bcast) : (tensor<3x4xf32>, tensor<3x4xf32>) -> tensor<3x4xf32>

    // Return the result
    return %out : tensor<3x4xf32>
  }
}
```

