Task: write a StableHLO program whose entry function has exactly this signature:
func.func @main(%x: tensor<3x5xf32>) -> tensor<6x6xf32>

It must compute: out has shape 6x6: x is placed so that out[i + 1, j + 0] = x[i, j], with 1 rows above, 2 rows below, 0 columns left and 1 columns right filled with the value -1.0.

Relevant operations: pad, constant.

Reply with the complete program in a single ```mlir code block.

```mlir
// StableHLO program to embed a 3x5 tensor into a 6x6 tensor with padding and fill values
module {
  func.func @main(%x: tensor<3x5xf32>) -> tensor<6x6xf32> {
    // Define the padding value constant: -1.0
    %pad_value = "stablehlo.constant"() {value = dense< -1.0 : f32 >} : () -> f32

    // Define the edge paddings:
    // For rows: 1 row above, 2 rows below, so edge_padding_low = [1], edge_padding_high = [2]
    // For columns: 0 left, 1 right, so edge_padding_low = [0], edge_padding_high = [1]
    // Since shape is 2D, combine into arrays
    %edge_padding_low = "stablehlo.constant"() {value = dense< [1_i64, 0_i64] >} : () -> tensor<2xi64>
    %edge_padding_high = "stablehlo.constant"() {value = dense< [2_i64, 1_i64] >} : () -> tensor<2xi64>
    // Interior padding is zero for all dimensions
    %interior_padding = "stablehlo.constant"() {value = dense< [0_i64, 0_i64] >} : () -> tensor<2xi64>

    // Pad the input tensor
    %padded = "stablehlo.pad"(%x, %pad_value)
      {edge_padding_low = %edge_padding_low,
       edge_padding_high = %edge_padding_high,
       interior_padding = %interior_padding} : (tensor<3x5xf32>, f32) -> tensor<6x6xf32>

    // Return the padded tensor
    return %padded : tensor<6x6xf32>
  }
}
